n.**\nSlot 15 sits *after* `ADVERSARIAL_REVIEW` and after `self._ibm.seal(...)` computes `bundle.bundle_hash` (`:355`). Any `docs/` or `ledger/` write L15 makes is **outside the bundle**, therefore outside the court's adjudication, outside the adversary's review, and not covered by the seal it gates. The dossier frames B's authority risk as role-scope only (a PLANNER holding `ledger/`). The structural problem is worse: L15 is a write channel into institutional memory positioned exactly where nothing can check it. Its \"Moderate\" implementability rating is too generous — B needs a design answer for *who verifies the ledger sync* before it is buildable at all.\n\n**Candidate C (L18 `MEMORY_UPDATE`) — the `_EVOLVE` defect is worse than described.**\nConfirmed: `write_scopes=(\"runtime/\", \"kernel/\")` on a `Role.PLANNER`. Additional, unnoted: the `RETROSPECT`/`EVOLVE` dispatches at `:217-218` sit **outside** `_run_body`'s `try/except BudgetExceeded` and **charge no budget** (no `budget.charge(result.cost)` on either call — compare `:270`). And the guard is `outcome.status in (RunStatus.SEALED, RunStatus.HALTED)` — so an unmetered stage with TCB write authority runs after every seal *and after every budget breach*, which is the state in which metering exists to intervene. This is a live economic-governance hole, not just an authority one.\n\n**On §0's self-refutation argument.** *\"I am, at this moment, executing L05 — the matrix refutes itself by the fact of this document's existence.\"* Invalid: this document is produced by `runtime/ade.py`, a **second, separate lifecycle** that dispatches RESEARCH → CRITIQUE → TRADEOFF out of band, ungated, with no relation to `_run_body`. The ADE's existence proves nothing about canonical L05. (The conclusion survives on independent evidence — `_run_body:258` — so §0's *finding* stands; its *argument* must not be inherited by TRADEOFF.) The deeper point: **there are two loops, and every candidate builds into the one that does not select what gets built.** Adding layers to `_run_body` leaves the ADE — the path currently deciding PAEOS's future — permanently outside the canonical chain. That is the largest unexamined architectural shortcut in the repository.\n\n---\n\n## §10. Verdicts\n\n| | Prerequisite for autonomous self-construction? | Blocking defect |\n|---|---|---|\n| **A · L07 MITIGATION** | **No, as scoped.** Yes only as an amended unit | Upstream L06 emits an intake, not a matrix (C3); neither anti-stub safeguard has an enforcement path (C5, C6); does not unblock the gate (C4) |\n| **B · L15 LEDGER_SYNC** | Not yet | Position places its writes outside every verification boundary (§9); ordering dependency on A stands |\n| **C · L18 MEMORY_UPDATE** | Not yet | Must repair `_EVOLVE` TCB write scope + unmetered post-seal dispatch first; that repair exceeds the layer (dossier agrees, and understates) |\n\n**The A → B → C ordering is correct. Its head is not A.**\n\n---\n\n## §11. Recommendation to TRADEOFF\n\n**Do not mint Candidate A as specified.** It would land a stage that receives no input, emits nothing durable, is bound by no gate, and satisfies an acceptance test that already passes — into a loop whose adversary is hardcoded to `PASS`. That is a ceremony layer, and by F3's own logic each subsequent audit will mark L07 done and move on.\n\nThe prerequisite work, in strict order, all of it cheaper than L07:\n\n1. **Give planner stages an output path.** `_CRITIQUE` needs a write scope (`critique/`), or `TaskResult.artifacts` needs a trace-derived fallback. Until then L09 is a no-op and no critique — including this one — can constrain any decision. *(Also, mechanically, the sole fix that makes the ADE's own `critique_result.artifacts` non-empty.)*\n2. **Repair the L06 output contract.** `_TRADEOFF` must emit a severity-ranked trade-off matrix into a scope of its own, distinct from the ADE's intake minting. This is also **F6** — the dossier concedes it *\"will block execution of whatever candidate is selected, including this one.\"* A conceded hard blocker is not a filing-cabinet item; it is the head of the path.\n3. **Wire `INTAKE` and `TRIAGE` as dispatched stages.** Closes `RE_DERIVE → IDEATE`, the first illegal edge, which no candidate touches.\n\nWith 1–3 landed, L07 becomes what the dossier claims it already is: a layer with a real input, a real consumer, and a checkable guard. Then A → B → C, then the gate.\n\nIf the charter forbids minting anything but a canonical layer this cycle, the defensible minimum is **L01 `INTAKE`** — a canonical layer, earlier in the chain, blocked by nothing, and the only one of the four that moves the gate. Selecting L07 over it requires an argument the dossier does not make.\n\n**Filed for DESIGN regardless of selection:** the `ChatBridgeRuntime` adversary bypass (`orchestrator:366`); planner `required_evidence` having no enforcement path; `RETROSPECT`/`EVOLVE` unmetered and outside the budget guard; L15's post-bundle write position; and the ADE/`_run_body` two-loop divergence.\n\n**Confidence.** High on C1–C7 and §9 — each traced to live source and, where executable, run. The one judgment call is §11's ranking of item 3 against items 1–2; all three are prerequisites, their relative order is arguable.","ttft_ms":1706,"ttft_stream_ms":945,"time_to_request_ms":36,"type":"result","duration_ms":263932,"uuid":"34bf4f50-b4b6-4217-88aa-e111d7662dc3"}
